# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <div v-for="i in 5">
    <div v-for="i in 5"></div>
  </div>
  <ul v-for="(item, index) in items">
    <li v-for="(child, index) in item.children">
      <span v-for="{ item } in child.entries">{{ item }}</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <div v-for="(value, key, position) in record">
    <div v-for="[key, position] in pairs"></div>
  </div>
  <div v-for="(row, row) in rows"></div>
</template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidNestedVFor.vue:4:17 lint/nursery/noVueTemplateShadow ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The template variable i hides a variable with the same name.
  
    2 │ <template>
    3 │   <div v-for="i in 5">
  > 4 │     <div v-for="i in 5"></div>
      │                 ^
    5 │   </div>
    6 │   <ul v-for="(item, index) in items">
  
  i The hidden i is declared here.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <div v-for="i in 5">
      │               ^
    4 │     <div v-for="i in 5"></div>
    5 │   </div>
  
  i Inside this element, i refers to the template variable, so the other i can't be used, and the two are easy to confuse.
  
  i Rename the template variable.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

